Bulk phonons, PBE without D3 (2026-10-02)

a-Beryllium (hcp, P6_3/mmc): 4x4x3 supercell (96 atoms), 7x7x9 Gamma k, job array 44153[]; path Gamma-K-M-Gamma-A-H-L-A-Gamma.
c0-Beryllium (bcc, Im-3m):   4x4x4 primitive supercell (64 atoms), 7x7x7 Gamma k, job array 44154[]; path Gamma-H-N-Gamma-P-H|P-N.
Geometries from 2.0_geometry_optimization/<structure>/CONTCAR (PBE, 27x27x27 k); +-0.01 A displacements; same INCAR as the
2D runs in this folder without the slab dipole correction.

Why: the published bulk phonons (3.0_phonon_dispersion, figures S3.13a and S3.13c) used PBE+D3 (IVDW = 12), and the "hcp"
run 3.0_phonon_dispersion/a-Beryllium_3 is not hcp at all: its POSCAR and DYNMAT are byte-identical to the 27-atom bcc
supercell c0-Beryllium_3 (only QPOINTS differs), so S3.13a showed bcc force constants on the hexagonal q path. The 250-atom
hcp attempt a-Beryllium_5 never finished.

Results (2026-10-02, both arrays exit 0):
- hcp: stable over the whole BZ, max 20.9 THz, Gamma optical modes 13.86 / 20.96 THz, residual force 3.7e-4 eV/A.
- bcc: harmonically unstable, -3.90 THz at N (commensurate with 4x4x4, exact for the supercell), min -3.72 THz on a 20^3
  mesh; expected for the high-temperature bcc phase. Figures S3.13a / S3.13c regenerated by 3.0_phonon_dispersion.ipynb.
